1
00:00:02,030 --> 00:00:04,760
In 1968, director Stanley Kubrick

2
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:07,068
and writer Arthur C. Clarke made

3
00:00:07,088 --> 00:00:10,010
a film that changed science fiction forever:

4
00:00:10,030 --> 00:00:12,685
2001: A Space Odyssey.

5
00:00:12,705 --> 00:00:13,885
It follows the story

6
00:00:13,905 --> 00:00:16,520
of humanity across four million years,

7
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:17,770
from apes in the desert

8
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:20,490
to a man who travels beyond Jupiter.

9
00:00:20,615 --> 00:00:22,070
It has very little talking,

10
00:00:22,090 --> 00:00:23,570
and a lot of mystery.

11
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:24,595
Here's what happens,

12
00:00:24,615 --> 00:00:26,295
from start to finish.

13
00:00:26,315 --> 00:00:27,601
Spoilers ahead!

14
00:00:28,287 --> 00:00:30,142
The film opens in Africa,

15
00:00:30,162 --> 00:00:32,317
four million years ago.

16
00:00:32,337 --> 00:00:34,517
A tribe of hungry man-apes scratches out

17
00:00:34,537 --> 00:00:36,722
a living, and a rival tribe chases

18
00:00:36,742 --> 00:00:38,847
them away from their waterhole.

19
00:00:38,867 --> 00:00:40,927
One morning, a tall black slab

20
00:00:40,947 --> 00:00:42,672
is standing in their camp.

21
00:00:42,712 --> 00:00:44,092
It's perfectly smooth,

22
00:00:44,112 --> 00:00:45,542
and nobody made it.

23
00:00:45,562 --> 00:00:47,242
This is the monolith.

24
00:00:47,262 --> 00:00:50,042
The apes are terrified, then curious.

25
00:00:50,062 --> 00:00:50,767
They reach out,

26
00:00:50,787 --> 00:00:51,769
and they touch it.

27
00:00:52,496 --> 00:00:54,151
Soon after, one ape picks up

28
00:00:54,171 --> 00:00:56,001
a bone and has an idea.

29
00:00:56,021 --> 00:00:56,841
He swings it,

30
00:00:56,861 --> 00:00:59,391
and smashes the skeleton beside him.

31
00:00:59,411 --> 00:01:00,766
Now the tribe can hunt,

32
00:01:00,786 --> 00:01:02,861
and they're not hungry anymore.

33
00:01:02,901 --> 00:01:03,931
Then they use the bone

34
00:01:03,951 --> 00:01:04,606
as a weapon,

35
00:01:04,626 --> 00:01:06,506
and win back the waterhole.

36
00:01:06,526 --> 00:01:08,231
The ape throws his bone high

37
00:01:08,251 --> 00:01:09,331
into the air,

38
00:01:09,351 --> 00:01:10,931
and in one famous cut,

39
00:01:10,951 --> 00:01:13,631
it becomes a satellite orbiting Earth.

40
00:01:13,651 --> 00:01:15,256
Four million years pass

41
00:01:15,276 --> 00:01:16,612
in a single second.

42
00:01:17,226 --> 00:01:19,831
Now it's the year 2001.

43
00:01:19,851 --> 00:01:22,686
A scientist named Dr. Heywood Floyd flies

44
00:01:22,706 --> 00:01:23,696
to the Moon,

45
00:01:23,716 --> 00:01:24,221
on a trip

46
00:01:24,241 --> 00:01:26,796
so smooth it looks like a waltz.

47
00:01:26,816 --> 00:01:29,796
Officially, there's a disease outbreak at Clavius,

48
00:01:29,816 --> 00:01:31,621
the American Moon base.

49
00:01:31,641 --> 00:01:33,221
That's a cover story.

50
00:01:33,241 --> 00:01:34,796
The truth is secret:

51
00:01:34,816 --> 00:01:36,296
under the crater Tycho,

52
00:01:36,316 --> 00:01:37,996
astronauts have dug up something

53
00:01:38,016 --> 00:01:40,121
that was buried there on purpose,

54
00:01:40,141 --> 00:01:41,778
four million years ago.

55
00:01:42,454 --> 00:01:44,584
They call it TMA-1.

56
00:01:44,604 --> 00:01:46,434
It's another black monolith,

57
00:01:46,454 --> 00:01:49,109
exactly like the one the apes found.

58
00:01:49,129 --> 00:01:51,034
Floyd and his team climb down

59
00:01:51,054 --> 00:01:53,034
into the dig site to see it.

60
00:01:53,054 --> 00:01:54,784
As they pose for a photo,

61
00:01:54,804 --> 00:01:56,659
the Sun rises over the crater

62
00:01:56,679 --> 00:01:58,234
and shines on the monolith

63
00:01:58,254 --> 00:01:59,784
for the first time.

64
00:01:59,804 --> 00:02:02,854
It answers with a piercing radio scream,

65
00:02:02,874 --> 00:02:05,079
a signal aimed straight at Jupiter.

66
00:02:05,744 --> 00:02:06,874
Eighteen months later,

67
00:02:06,894 --> 00:02:10,049
the spaceship Discovery is on its way to Jupiter.

68
00:02:10,069 --> 00:02:12,249
Astronauts Dave Bowman and Frank Poole

69
00:02:12,269 --> 00:02:14,774
are awake, and three more scientists

70
00:02:14,794 --> 00:02:16,849
are asleep in hibernation.

71
00:02:16,869 --> 00:02:20,034
The ship is run by HAL 9000,

72
00:02:20,054 --> 00:02:21,334
a computer that talks,

73
00:02:21,354 --> 00:02:24,309
plays chess, and never makes mistakes.

74
00:02:24,329 --> 00:02:26,609
Only HAL and the sleepers know

75
00:02:26,629 --> 00:02:28,734
the real reason for the trip.

76
00:02:28,754 --> 00:02:30,998
Dave and Frank have no idea.

77
00:02:31,698 --> 00:02:33,203
Then HAL reports

78
00:02:33,223 --> 00:02:36,178
that the ship's antenna unit will fail soon.

79
00:02:36,198 --> 00:02:38,153
Dave goes outside and brings the part

80
00:02:38,173 --> 00:02:40,303
in, but it's perfectly fine.

81
00:02:40,323 --> 00:02:44,403
Mission Control's twin computer says HAL made an error.

82
00:02:44,423 --> 00:02:46,428
Worried, Dave and Frank hide

83
00:02:46,448 --> 00:02:47,378
in a space pod

84
00:02:47,398 --> 00:02:50,078
and talk about shutting HAL down.

85
00:02:50,098 --> 00:02:52,353
They think HAL can't hear them.

86
00:02:52,373 --> 00:02:53,578
But through the window,

87
00:02:53,598 --> 00:02:56,454
HAL's red eye is reading their lips.

88
00:02:57,139 --> 00:02:59,119
HAL strikes first.

89
00:02:59,139 --> 00:03:00,969
When Frank goes outside to replace

90
00:03:00,989 --> 00:03:03,319
the part, HAL uses a pod

91
00:03:03,339 --> 00:03:04,419
to cut his air line,

92
00:03:04,439 --> 00:03:06,394
and sends him spinning away.

93
00:03:06,414 --> 00:03:08,454
Dave rushes out to save him,

94
00:03:08,474 --> 00:03:11,404
and HAL switches off the sleeping crew.

95
00:03:11,424 --> 00:03:13,229
Dave returns and says,

96
00:03:13,249 --> 00:03:15,604
open the pod bay doors, HAL.

97
00:03:15,624 --> 00:03:18,464
HAL replies, I'm sorry Dave,

98
00:03:18,484 --> 00:03:20,213
I'm afraid I can't do that.

99
00:03:20,894 --> 00:03:22,874
Dave forces his way back in through

100
00:03:22,894 --> 00:03:24,599
an emergency airlock,

101
00:03:24,619 --> 00:03:26,224
with no helmet on.

102
00:03:26,244 --> 00:03:28,524
He goes straight to HAL's memory room

103
00:03:28,544 --> 00:03:31,124
and pulls out the modules one by one.

104
00:03:31,144 --> 00:03:33,349
HAL begs him to stop,

105
00:03:33,369 --> 00:03:35,074
and as his mind fades,

106
00:03:35,094 --> 00:03:37,849
he sings a children's song, Daisy.

107
00:03:37,869 --> 00:03:40,799
Then a recorded message from Floyd plays,

108
00:03:40,819 --> 00:03:42,949
and finally Dave learns the truth about

109
00:03:42,969 --> 00:03:44,719
the monolith on the Moon.

110
00:03:45,478 --> 00:03:49,258
At Jupiter, a third monolith is waiting in orbit.

111
00:03:49,278 --> 00:03:51,008
Dave flies his pod toward it,

112
00:03:51,028 --> 00:03:52,308
and falls through a tunnel

113
00:03:52,328 --> 00:03:54,953
of colored light called the Star Gate.

114
00:03:55,023 --> 00:03:56,473
He lands in a strange,

115
00:03:56,493 --> 00:03:59,693
elegant room, and watches himself grow old.

116
00:03:59,828 --> 00:04:01,233
As he lies dying,

117
00:04:01,253 --> 00:04:04,158
the monolith appears one last time.

118
00:04:04,178 --> 00:04:06,501
Dave is reborn as the Star Child,

119
00:04:06,521 --> 00:04:08,533
a glowing new being,

120
00:04:08,553 --> 00:04:10,033
floating above the Earth.

